// PersonaLive end-of-turn detection contract. cored calls Predict with the
// AUDIO of the user's just-finished utterance (16 kHz mono float32 LE PCM, the
// last <=8 s) and gets back P(end-of-turn): high = the user finished, low =
// they're likely still going — cored holds the turn open and coalesces the next
// utterance instead of answering prematurely. Judging the waveform (intonation,
// pace, trailing fillers) rather than the transcript is both more robust and
// runs in parallel with ASR. The reference worker runs Smart Turn (Pipecat,
// BSD-2 — an audio semantic VAD), but the slot is PLUGGABLE: any worker that
// speaks this contract works (or none — then cored answers every utterance).
// Unary (not streaming): one quick call per finished utterance, off the hot
